{
  "summary": "Supplies fresh randomness via GetRandHash() instead of all zeros as the BIP340 auxiliary data parameter when creating Schnorr signatures in MutableTransactionSignatureCreator. Adapts bip341_keypath_test_vectors to assert non-deterministic but valid signatures, and seeds the RNG in the script_sign fuzz target.",
  "problem": "Taproot Schnorr signatures are generated with static all-zero auxiliary data, leaving signing operations without the defense-in-depth side-channel and fault-injection resistance recommended by BIP340.",
  "evidence": [
    "BIP340 specification recommends fresh randomness in auxiliary data to harden nonce generation against side channels and fault injection (quoted in description and commit message).",
    "Fixes open issue #31883 ('SignatureCreator should supply auxiliary data argument for additional bip340 signature security')."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Diff is small (+24/-5) across signing, test, and fuzzing code. Makes Schnorr transaction signing non-deterministic.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Bitcoin Core currently passes all-zero auxiliary data when signing Taproot inputs. This PR changes MutableTransactionSignatureCreator to pass fresh randomness from GetRandHash(), adhering to the BIP340 recommendation to protect against side-channel attacks and fault injection during signature generation. It also updates BIP341 keypath unit tests to handle non-deterministic signatures and seeds the RNG in script_sign fuzzing. This resolves issue #31883.",
